        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>Result</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::Result</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Production-ready <ref refid="namespacethemis_1a8fb070bff85b6d9e11b92dd7985e2c2b" kindref="member">Result&lt;T&gt;</ref> type alias using <ref refid="classtl_1_1expected" kindref="compound">tl::expected</ref></para>
<para>This provides:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Zero-overhead error propagation (no exceptions)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Type-safe error handling (compiler-enforced checking)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Composable error handling with monadic operations</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Forward-compatible with C++23 std::expected</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Usage examples:</para>
<para>// Function returning <ref refid="namespacethemis_1a8fb070bff85b6d9e11b92dd7985e2c2b" kindref="member">Result</ref> <ref refid="namespacethemis_1a8fb070bff85b6d9e11b92dd7985e2c2b" kindref="member">Result&lt;std::string&gt;</ref> readFile(const std::string&amp; path) { if (!fileExists(path)) { return <ref refid="classtl_1_1unexpected" kindref="compound">tl::unexpected(Error(ErrorCode::ERR_STORAGE_FILE_NOT_FOUND, path))</ref>; } return fileContents; }</para>
<para>// Caller checking result auto result = readFile(&quot;config.yaml&quot;); if (result) { processContent(*result); } else { spdlog::error(&quot;Failed to read file: {}&quot;, result.error().message()); }</para>
<para>// Monadic error propagation return readFile(path) .and_then([](const std::string&amp; content) { return parseYaml(content); }) .and_then([](const Config&amp; cfg) { return validateConfig(cfg); }); </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/utils/expected.h" line="333" column="1" bodyfile="include/utils/expected.h" bodystart="333" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
